      "title": "Nvidia’s Jensen Huang expected to testify before Congress amid calls for crackdown on China chip exports – live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/live/2026/nov/13/nvidia-jensen-huang-to-testify-before-congress-live-latest-updates",
      "description": "<p>Huang’s resignation has sent shockwaves through the AI industry, after revelations of extramarital affairs, including one involving a suspected Chinese spy</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/12/nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-resigns\"><strong>Full report: Jensen Huang resigns as Nvidia CEO</strong></a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/12/jensen-huang-built-an-ai-kingdom-now-hes-gone-will-nvidias-ramparts-be-breached\"><strong>Analysis: Jensen Huang built an AI kingdom. Now he’s gone, will Nvidia’s ramparts be breached?</strong></a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Can the AI economy survive without its “central bank”? What does Jensen Huang’s fall mean for the world’s second-most valuable company, and what might a tremor in its fortunes mean for the world?</strong></p><p>Nvidia’s sky-high valuation is based on the fact that it designs and sells the advanced AI chips, called graphics processing units (GPUs), that underpin the AI economy. Without these, AI models such as <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/chatgpt\">ChatGPT</a> and Claude could not be trained and would not run.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/live/2026/nov/13/nvidia-jensen-huang-to-testify-before-congress-live-latest-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-13T03:36:05"
    },
    {
      "title": "Who is Colette Kress, interim Nvidia CEO after Jensen Huang exit?",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/12/jensen-huang-nvidia-ceo-replacement",
      "description": "<p>Chief financial officer, reportedly disparaged by Huang during summer meeting, to take over on short-term basis</p><p>The hunt is on for a new Nvidia CEO. It comes after a whirlwind week, which saw the company head and co-founder, Jensen Huang, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/12/nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-resigns\">resign amid multiple allegations of extramarital affairs</a>, including one that involved an alleged Chinese spy and two with company employees.</p><p>Nvidia immediately named Colette Kress, the company’s chief financial officer, as the interim CEO. It’s possible she could stay on permanently, but the company could also name another candidate for the full-time role. Names that have been floated include Ian Buck, who manages Nvidia’s AI hardware and software products, and Rene Haas, a former Nvidia employee and the current CEO of Arm Holdings, a UK-based chipmaker.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/12/jensen-huang-nvidia-ceo-replacement\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-13T03:02:06"
    },
