      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/jensen-huang-quits-as-nvidia-ceo-amid-affair-spy-allegations-what-we-know-126111300019_1.html",
      "description": "Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang has resigned from his top post at the chipmaker he co-founded, after reports of the tech titan's extramarital affairs came into the spotlight this week.\nOne of those relationships has raised national security concerns. The New York Times reported that Huang had an affair with a businesswoman US intelligence suspects to be a Chinese spy, which Beijing denies.\nSeparately, the outlet and later others found Huang was said to have had another affair with an Nvidia executive who reported to him directly - compounding calls for him to step down.\nNvidia announced Huang's resignation on Thursday, effective immediately. The California-based company said that Colette Kress - who has been Nvidia's chief financial officer and executive vice president since 2013 - will step into the role of interim CEO.\nThe scandal marks the most tumultuous chapter yet for Nvidia, whose high-end chips have emerged as the leading building blocks for artificial intelligence. Huang himself h",
